<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abraham Fischer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1850–1913</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abraham Fischer was a politician of the Orange Free State and its successor, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orange-river-colony">Orange River Colony</a>. He served on the Free State executive and as one of its envoys to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-boer-war">Second Boer War</a>. When responsible government was granted in 1907 he became prime minister at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orangia-unie">Orangia Unie</a> party, and after 1910 he was a minister in the first Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> cabinet.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abraham-fischer.jpg" alt="Abraham Fischer" width="234" height="336" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boer_Legation_VA0949.jpg: Atelier Straugh, formerly Kameke, Javastraat 20, The Hague, The Netherlands Original upload... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abraham_Fischer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
